### A5. Data model (Firestore)

All money values are integers in kobo (1 NGN = 100 kobo). Never store floats for money.

Collections:

`categories/{categoryId}`
- slug (string, unique), name, description, heroImage (storage path), order (number), visible (boolean), themeOverride (optional object)

`products/{productId}`
- slug (string, unique), name, brand, categoryId, status ("draft" | "published" | "archived")
- priceKobo (int, VAT inclusive), compareAtKobo (int, optional, shows as strike-through)
- stockQty (int), stockStatus (derived: "in_stock" | "low" | "out")
- warrantyMonths (int), warrantyTerms (string, per product)
- shortDescription, longDescription (rich text, sanitized)
- images (array of { path, alt, width, height, order })
- specs (map keyed by spec field id, values typed per the category schema)
- tags (array of strings), audienceTags (array: "retail" | "education" | "bulk")
- createdAt, updatedAt, updatedBy

`specSchemas/{categoryId}`
- fields (ordered array of { id, label, type: "text" | "number" | "boolean" | "list", unit?, required, group })
- Laptops example fields: processor, ramGb, storageGb, storageType, display, graphics, battery, ports, os, weightKg, warranty
- Printers example fields: printType, colorMode, maxPaperSize, printSpeedPpm, connectivity, duplex, tonerOrInk
- Scanners example fields: scanType, dpi, sheetFeeder, dutyCycle, connectivity

`discounts/{discountId}`
- code (string, optional, uppercase, unique when present)
- type ("percent" | "fixed_kobo")
- value (number; basis points for percent, e.g. 1000 = 10%)
- scope ("cart" | "category" | "product")
- scopeIds (array)
- minSubtotalKobo (int)
- maxUses (int, optional), usedCount (int)
- startsAt, endsAt (timestamps)
- active (boolean), audienceTags (optional)

`settings/theme` (CMS tier)
- colors (map of token names to hex)
- typography (fontDisplay, fontBody, scale, weights)
- spacing (scale base, section padding)
- layout (containerWidthPx, radiusPx)
- motion (level: "off" | "subtle" | "full")
- filters (grainOpacity, blurIntensity)
- version (number)

`settings/site` (CMS tier and assets tier)
- tier ("assets" | "cms")
- businessName, whatsappNumber, email, address, hours
- vatRate (0.075), currency ("NGN")
- deliveryZones (array of { id, label, feeKobo, etaDays, notes })
- segmentCopy (object keyed by segment id)
- footerCopy, announcementBar (optional)

`orders/{orderRef}` (ref format: IR-XXXXXX, 6 characters from an unambiguous alphabet)
- status ("pending_payment" | "paid" | "pending_whatsapp" | "confirmed" | "fulfilled" | "cancelled" | "refunded")
- channel ("paystack" | "whatsapp")
- items (array of { productId, nameSnapshot, unitPriceKobo, qty, lineTotalKobo })
- subtotalKobo, discountKobo, deliveryKobo, vatKobo (informational breakdown), totalKobo
- discountCode (optional), deliveryZoneId, customer { name, phone, email, address, state, country }
- paystackReference (optional), createdAt, updatedAt
- Customers do not need an account. Orders are reachable via reference plus contact.

`carts` are not stored in Firestore for guests. The cart lives in Zustand with localStorage persistence. The server recalculates everything at checkout.

`admins` is not a collection. Admin authority lives in Firebase Auth custom claims: { role: "assets" | "cms" | "owner" }.

### A6. Pricing and money rules

- Price is stored VAT inclusive. VAT component for display: vatKobo = round(priceKobo - priceKobo / (1 + vatRate)).
- Line total = unitPriceKobo * qty. No float math anywhere.
- Discounts apply in this order: product-level, then category-level, then cart-level. Percent discounts round down to the nearest kobo. Fixed discounts never exceed the eligible subtotal.
- A discount is valid only if: active, within the date window, below maxUses, meets minSubtotalKobo, and matches scope and audience.
- The server (/api/price) is the source of truth for totals. The client displays the server response and never trusts its own numbers at checkout.
- Delivery fee comes from settings.deliveryZones. Pickup at Ikeja is a zone with feeKobo 0.
- Display format: en-NG currency, no decimals for whole naira, two decimals only when kobo is non-zero.

### A7. Cart behavior

- Zustand store with persist middleware, key "ir-cart-v1". Stores: items (productId, qty, addedAt), discountCode, deliveryZoneId, sessionId (anonymous UUID generated once).
- Adding an item: clamps qty to stockQty. Shows a toast if clamped.
- Cart drawer slides in with spring-like easing. Quantity changes trigger a debounced call to /api/price (250 ms). Totals animate with a rolling counter.
- Stale-item handling: if a product is archived or out of stock at price time, the line is marked and the user is told before checkout.
- Discount code entry calls /api/price with the code; the response includes applied amount and a human reason string.
- The cart is never the source of truth. Refreshing the page re-fetches prices.

### A8. Checkout flow

Two channels, both presented equally with clear labels:

1. Pay online (Paystack)
   - Step 1: customer details (name, phone, email, delivery state, address)
   - Step 2: /api/order/create validates the cart, recalculates with /api/price logic, creates an order doc in "pending_payment", and calls Paystack initialize with amount in kobo and metadata.orderRef.
   - Step 3: redirect or inline Paystack popup. On success callback, client calls /api/order/verify with the reference.
   - Step 4: /api/order/verify calls Paystack verify, checks status, amount matches totalKobo exactly, currency is NGN, then sets order to "paid" using the Admin SDK.
   - Paystack webhook /api/paystack/webhook validates the x-paystack-signature header (HMAC SHA512 of raw body with PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY), then performs the same verification, idempotently.
   - Never mark an order paid from the client alone.

2. Order on WhatsApp
   - Same details form, then /api/order/create with channel "whatsapp" creates the order as "pending_whatsapp".
   - The client opens wa.me/2349046453977 with a prefilled message: order reference, itemized list with qty and kobo-converted naira totals, delivery zone, and customer name.
   - Admin sees pending WhatsApp orders in the Assets module and marks them confirmed or cancelled.

Both paths end on /order/:ref with a receipt (status, items, VAT breakdown, delivery zone, warranty summary per item).

